{"id":"evt_fc04nyka","issue_id":"eavs-sth0","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-06-10T07:52:30.765187019Z","changes":[{"field":"description","from":"## Summary\n\n~~Extend eavs with credential proxying~~ -- REVISED: the proxy endpoint belongs on **oqto-runner**, not eavs.\n\nEavs is a shared central service. kyz vaults are per-user. The runner already runs as the target user and has access to their kyz vault. The credential proxy naturally lives on the runner.\n\n```\neavs  = LLM proxy       (shared, multi-user, central)\nrunner = agent lifecycle + credential proxy  (per-user, has vault access)\nkyz   = encrypted vault  (per-user, storage only)\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nAgent -> runner /v1/proxy -> runner reads user's kyz -> inject cred -> target API\n         (per-user process)  (user's own vault)\n         \nAgent -> eavs /v1/chat/completions -> LLM providers    (unchanged)\n```\n\n## Runner Proxy API\n\n```\nPOST /v1/proxy\n{\n  \"url\": \"https://api.stripe.com/v1/charges\",\n  \"method\": \"POST\",\n  \"headers\": {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n  \"body\": {\"amount\": 2000, \"currency\": \"usd\"},\n  \"credential\": {\n    \"ref\": \"stripe/api-key/value\",   // kyz service/key/field\n    \"inject\": \"bearer\"               // bearer | basic | header:X-Api-Key | query:key | body:api_key\n  }\n}\n\nResponse: upstream API response passed through (status, headers, body)\n```\n\n```\nGET /v1/credentials\nReturns metadata only (service, key, field names, pinned hosts). Never values.\n```\n\n## Security\n\n- Runner runs as the target user -- natural access to their kyz vault\n- Secret values never returned to agent (structurally impossible)\n- Host pinning, SSRF protection, redirect auth stripping\n- Audit log: JSONL with timestamp, session ID, target URL, credential ref, HTTP status\n\n## Integration\n\n- Runner already exposes a socket to the agent (runner protocol)\n- Add /v1/proxy and /v1/credentials to that socket\n- Runner injects CREDENTIAL_PROXY_URL into agent env\n- Pi skill or MCP tool wraps the call for agent ergonomics\n\n## Note\n\nThis issue is now misplaced in the eavs repo -- should be moved to oqto-runner. Keeping here for traceability until moved.","to":"Generalize secret resolution: a SecretProvider trait + registry keyed on a ref scheme, reusing eavs's existing provider-prefix pattern (resolved_api_key already does env:/keychain:/literal). A secret ref is '<scheme>:<path>', dispatched to a backend, resolved value cached with a TTL, never logged. kyz is the FIRST provider (byteowlz default for oqto); the injection engine and config are backend-agnostic. Env/file schemes serve dev. Additional backends are a separate child. This is the resolution layer the substitution engine (eavs-w6wg.3) calls."}]}
