{"id":"evt_vtm55kwn","issue_id":"eavs-w6wg","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-06-10T07:53:11.746434580Z","changes":[{"field":"description","from":"Layer credential injection onto the transparent egress proxy (eavs-frd8, now complete). Today the transparent listener does capture + allow/deny + splice (passthrough); it never sees inside TLS, so it cannot inject secrets. This epic adds selective MITM for explicitly-configured hosts so the agent only ever holds PLACEHOLDER tokens while eavs substitutes the real credential at the transport layer for the matching allowlisted host -- the gondolin createHttpHooks model, backed by the kyz vault.\n\nInvariant: the real secret NEVER enters the agent (env, memory, fs). The agent env carries a high-entropy placeholder; eavs swaps in the real value only for the destination that secret is scoped to, only after TLS termination, and blocks any real value heading to a non-allowlisted host (anti-exfil).\n\nScope boundaries:\n- MITM only the hosts configured for injection; everything else stays splice/passthrough (preserves perf and does not break cert-pinned clients).\n- HTTP(S) only (placeholder substitution needs a request to rewrite). SSH/DB wire protocols are out of scope.\n- Cross-repo touchpoint: the agent must trust eavs's MITM CA -- oqto-sandbox installs it into the agent's trust store / SSL_CERT_FILE; eavs generates/serves the CA.\n\nReference: external-repos/gondolin/host/src/http/hooks.ts (createHttpHooks, applySecretsToRequest, assertSecretValuesAllowedForHost). Builds on the transparent listener in src/transparent.rs.\n\nDefinition of done: an agent holding a placeholder reaches an allowlisted host through eavs, the real kyz-resolved credential is injected and upstream returns 200; the same placeholder/real value sent to a non-allowlisted host is blocked; secrets never appear in logs or the agent; audit records every injection.","to":"Layer credential injection onto the transparent egress proxy (eavs-frd8, now complete). Today the transparent listener does capture + allow/deny + splice (passthrough); it never sees inside TLS, so it cannot inject secrets. This epic adds selective MITM for explicitly-configured hosts so the client only ever holds PLACEHOLDER tokens while eavs substitutes the real credential at the transport layer for the matching allowlisted host -- the gondolin createHttpHooks model, backed by a PLUGGABLE secret-provider interface (kyz is one backend among Vault/Infisical/Bitwarden/1Password/cloud; see eavs-sth0).\n\nInvariant: the real secret NEVER enters the client (env, memory, fs). The client env carries a high-entropy placeholder; eavs swaps in the real value only for the destination that secret is scoped to, only after TLS termination, and blocks any real value heading to a non-allowlisted host (anti-exfil).\n\nScope boundaries:\n- MITM only the hosts configured for injection; everything else stays splice/passthrough (preserves perf and does not break cert-pinned clients).\n- HTTP(S) only (placeholder substitution needs a request to rewrite). SSH/DB wire protocols are out of scope.\n- Secret backend is pluggable and backend-agnostic in the injection path; no provider is privileged.\n- Cross-repo touchpoint kept thin: the consumer (e.g. oqto-sandbox) must trust eavs's MITM CA -- eavs publishes the CA; the consumer installs it into its client trust store. The oqto-specific install logic lives on the oqto side, not in eavs.\n\nReference: external-repos/gondolin/host/src/http/hooks.ts (createHttpHooks, applySecretsToRequest, assertSecretValuesAllowedForHost). Builds on the transparent listener in src/transparent.rs.\n\nDefinition of done: a client holding a placeholder reaches an allowlisted host through eavs, the real (provider-resolved) credential is injected and upstream returns 200; the same placeholder/real value sent to a non-allowlisted host is blocked; secrets never appear in logs or on the client; audit records every injection."}]}
{"id":"evt_zww4ebpg","issue_id":"eavs-w6wg.3","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-06-10T07:53:11.759609866Z","changes":[{"field":"description","from":"Port the gondolin secret model (external-repos/gondolin/host/src/http/hooks.ts). Per secret: a high-entropy placeholder (the agent's env value) + a host allowlist + the real value (from kyz). On a terminated request: replace placeholder->real in headers (and optionally URL query) ONLY when the request host matches that secret's allowlist; inject at the last moment after any rewriting. Anti-exfil: assertSecretValuesAllowedForHost -- block a request already carrying a real secret value bound for a non-allowlisted host (redirect hops). Keep SSRF/internal-range blocks. Unit-testable as a pure request->request transform. Blocked by config schema + kyz resolution.","to":"Port the gondolin secret model (external-repos/gondolin/host/src/http/hooks.ts). Per secret: a high-entropy placeholder (the client's env value) + a host allowlist + the real value resolved via the pluggable secret-provider interface (eavs-sth0; kyz or any other backend). On a terminated request: replace placeholder->real in headers (and optionally URL query) ONLY when the request host matches that secret's allowlist; inject at the last moment after any rewriting. Anti-exfil: assertSecretValuesAllowedForHost -- block a request already carrying a real secret value bound for a non-allowlisted host (redirect hops). Keep SSRF/internal-range blocks. Unit-testable as a pure request->request transform. Blocked by config schema + the secret-provider interface."}]}
