{"id":"evt_yj34bjda","issue_id":"eavs-sk8z","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-07-22T07:42:30.016141111Z","harness":"pi","harness_session_id":"019f7fa4-ce7a-7c28-b107-c7b9f3b37ae3","session_name":"eavs: Any Updates From External-repospi-mono We Need [void-pull-itch]","model":"claude-bridge/claude-opus-4-8","changes":[{"field":"description","from":null,"to":"Virtual-key cost accounting undercounts cache-heavy workloads and mis-prices unknown models.\n\nRoot causes:\n- UsageTracker only captures cache_read_input_tokens; cache_creation (write) tokens are dropped, so Anthropic prompt-cache writes (billed 1.25x input) are billed as normal input.\n- keys/pricing.rs ModelPricing has only cached_input_cost_per_token (read); no cache_write field. Rates come from a small hand-maintained embedded table, so unknown models fall back to guesses (and a flat 50% cached-read discount that is wrong for Anthropic ~10%).\n- calculate_cost_with_cache does input-cached unconditionally; correct for OpenAI (inclusive) but wrong for Anthropic (input already excludes cache).\n\nFix:\n- Source rates from models.dev CatalogCost (already deserialized: input/output/cache_read/cache_write, in USD/1M tokens). Add cache_write_cost_per_token to ModelPricing; populate from catalog (÷1e6).\n- Convention from data: cache_write present -> Anthropic-style, bill creation tokens at cache_write; absent/0 -> OpenAI-style, no separate write cost.\n- Capture cache_creation_input_tokens in UsageTracker; thread through update_usage; add usage_history.cache_write_tokens column (idempotent migration).\n- Provider-aware input handling: do not subtract cache from Anthropic input; subtract only for inclusive (OpenAI) convention.\n- cost = regular_input*input + cache_read*read_rate + cache_write*write_rate + output*output.\n\nAlso: CLI cost-overview commands (per owner/user and per key: tokens + costs)."}]}
