{"id":"evt_nx29qayz","issue_id":"eavs-yxp7","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:48:08.216467333Z","harness":"pi","harness_session_id":"019fb7b5-a2cc-73a6-9a15-1af85bd6955c","session_name":"eavs: Implement TRX Owner Labels [posh-high-hits]","model":"Z-AI/glm-5.2","changes":[{"field":"description","from":null,"to":"`KeyStore::delete_key` runs `DELETE FROM virtual_keys WHERE key_hash = ?`. The `usage_history` table declares `FOREIGN KEY (key_hash) REFERENCES virtual_keys(key_hash) ON DELETE CASCADE`. sqlx 0.8 enables `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` by default (verified: a pool connection reports foreign_keys=1), so the CASCADE fires and every usage_history row for that key is deleted on hard delete.\n\nImpact: cost/usage history (and therefore owner rollups) is silently destroyed when a key is hard-deleted. This contradicts the eavs-5gf3 design goal that rollups \"survive key deletion\". For a billing/cost feature, losing history on key purge is almost never desirable.\n\nScope note: the routine production path is `disable_key` (soft delete, used by DELETE /admin/keys/:id), which preserves history — so this only bites the currently-dead-code `delete_key` method. But it should be correct before delete_key is wired up or relied upon.\n\nDiscovered while writing the eavs-5gf3 \"survive key deletion\" regression test.\n\nFix options to evaluate:\n- Drop the ON DELETE CASCADE from the usage_history FK (preserve history on hard delete). SQLite cannot ALTER an existing FK constraint, so existing DBs need a table-rebuild migration; fresh DBs only need the CREATE TABLE changed.\n- Or make delete_key re-point/anonymize usage rows (set key_hash to a tombstone) before deleting the key.\n- Or document delete_key as intentionally destructive and gate it behind a --force/--purge flag.\n\nHow to proof a positive outcome:\n- New test: create key with owner, record usage, delete_key(&h), assert get_usage_by_owner still returns the owner's bucket with the recorded usage (and get_usage_by_key returns key_id=\"\" with owner preserved).\n- Migration test: a pre-existing keys.db (with the CASCADE FK baked in) must still roll up history after delete_key post-migration.\n- Regression: existing test_owner_rollup_survives_key_deletion soft-delete branch still passes; disable_key still preserves history."}]}
